          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{2(x+3)}{3}-\\frac{3x}{2}&\\ge 3\\\\4(x+3)-9x&\\ge 18\\\\4x+12-9x&\\ge 18\\\\-5x+12&\\ge 18\\\\-5x&\\ge 6\\\\x&\\le-\\frac{6}{5}\\end{align*}$$\nThe direction reverses when dividing by $-5$. A closed endpoint at $-\\frac{6}{5}$ has a ray to the left.",
